 {:entry/name        "Beleriand"
  :entry/type        :entry.type/place
  :entry/description "The name was said to have signified the country of _Balar_, and to have been given at first to the lands about the mouths of _Sirion_ that faced the _Isle of Balar_. Later the name spread to include all the ancient coast of the Northwest of _Middle-earth_ south of the Firth of _Drengist_, and all the inner lands south of _Hithlum_ and eastwards to the feet of the _Blue Mountains_, divided by the river _Sirion_ into East and West Beleriand. Beleriand was broken in the turmoils at the end of the _First Age_, and invaded by the sea, so that only _Ossiriand_ (_Lindon_) remained."
  :entry/page        [110 111 112 113 114 115 241 273 274]
  :entry/appears-in  [[:chapter/name "Of Beleriand and its Realms"]
